From f3af8edc21dac8a1fd97380930970773ab523336 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:39:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 420/423] Design check: short thread engagement, ignored pairs
 not measured, tiny edges of imported shapes

A screw in a threaded hole is now also checked for its length in the hole:
at least 0.8 x its diameter (a nut's height) or all of a shorter hole; a
warning per pair of parts with the number of screws and the shortest.
The pairs given to ignore and the parts of one item are left out of the
measuring as well, not only of the report. Shapes without a history (an
imported STEP, a shape set by a script) are not checked for tiny edges:
there is nothing to fix in them (tiny_edge_imported=True checks them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
